"Fill in the Predicted \\(a\\) column of the Gaps table. For a period ratio \\(r\\), the asteroid’s period is \\(P = 11.86/r\\) years, and Kepler’s third law gives its distance \\(a = P^{2/3}\\) AU (on most calculators, type P ^ ({#}/{#})). Compare each prediction with the gap in the real asteroids. How close are they?",
"In Part {#}, which asteroids had their orbits stretched until they crossed Mars’s orbit, and how long did it take? Which stayed calm?",
